      "title": "Plug-in solar panels could save households up to $370 a year – if Australia made them legal as in the UK",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/29/plug-in-solar-panels-could-save-households-370-a-year-and-experts-say-australia-should-copy-the-uk-in-legalising-them",
      "description": "<p>A plug-in solar kit that costs about $1,000 ‘pays for itself in three years’, one expert says</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Millions of Australians could be saving up to $370 a year on energy bills and doing their bit for the climate crisis if Labor followed the UK’s lead in legalising plug-in solar panels, an advocacy group has said.</p><p>Plug-in solar refers to small standalone solar units that could be attached to balconies or used in back yards and plugged into power points, offsetting the energy used by household appliances.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/29/plug-in-solar-panels-could-save-households-370-a-year-and-experts-say-australia-should-copy-the-uk-in-legalising-them\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-29T05:13:27"
    },
    {
      "title": "What we know about the Australians missing in the Nepal floods",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/29/what-we-know-about-the-australians-missing-in-the-nepal-floods",
      "description": "<p>More than 40 Australians are among several thousand people unaccounted for after catastrophic flooding on the Nepal-Tibet border</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/27/nepal-tibet-flash-flood-visual-guide-why-how-flooding-happened-floods-cause-reason-explained\">How the deadly Nepal and Tibet flash flood unfolded – a visual guide</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>An 11-year-old child, an ADF member and many other pilgrims and trekkers have been named <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/28/family-missing-australians-nepal-tibet-flash-floods\">among the Australians</a> missing after deadly flash floods and landslides tore through valleys on the Nepal-Tibet border.</p><p>As of Saturday there were 41 Australians among almost 2,500 people reported missing in the disaster, including at least 777 foreigners. At least 93,000 people were estimated to have been affected by the disaster, according to the Red Cross.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/29/what-we-know-about-the-australians-missing-in-the-nepal-floods\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-29T03:54:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Nepal-Tibet floods: Nepal calls for technical support for rescue efforts as number of missing rises to nearly 3,000 – latest updates",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-floods-latest-updates-death-toll-missing-search-and-rescue",
      "description": "<p>Nepali government says India and China are sending expert tunnel rescue teams, as minister estimates cost of rebuilding could be billions of dollars</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2026/aug/28/the-flood-took-everything-i-have-survivors-grieve-for-relatives-and-homes-swept-away-in-nepal\">‘The flood took everything I have’: survivors grieve for relatives and homes swept away in Nepal</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-chinese-rescue-team-finds-nothing-but-ruins-after-reaching-border-crossing-hit-by-deadly-flood\">Chinese rescuers find ‘nothing but ruins’ at border crossing as Nepal seeks help to ID and store the dead</a></p></li></ul><p>Outside the army camp in the Nuwakot district of Nepal, people run their fingers down the sheets of paper pinned to the wall, scanning the growing list of those reported missing for news of loved ones. <strong>Nepali authorities said nearly 3,000 people are missing,</strong> while China reported <strong>more than 550 people unaccounted for.</strong></p><p>Nepal’s foreign minister, <strong>Shisir Khanal,</strong> has appealed for international support to help rebuild the country after the floods, saying reconstruction efforts could run into <strong>“billions of dollars”</strong> AFP reports.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-floods-latest-updates-death-toll-missing-search-and-rescue\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-29T15:32:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "Number of missing in Nepal and Tibet rises to nearly 3,000 as operations continue",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-chinese-rescue-team-finds-nothing-but-ruins-after-reaching-border-crossing-hit-by-deadly-flood",
      "description": "<p>Nepal requests foreign ⁠help in identification and storing of bodies, DNA testing and rescuing people from tunnels</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/27/nepal-tibet-flash-flood-visual-guide-why-how-flooding-happened-floods-cause-reason-explained\">Visual guide: how the deadly flooding unfolded</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-floods-latest-updates-death-toll-missing-search-and-rescue\">Nepal-Tibet flash flood – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The number of people killed in the floods in Nepal has risen to at least 675, the country’s disaster authority has said.</p><p>Seven have also been confirmed dead in Tibet by Chinese state media, taking the total killed when a glacial collapse unleashed a deadly torrent through river systems in the Himalayan mountains to 682.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-chinese-rescue-team-finds-nothing-but-ruins-after-reaching-border-crossing-hit-by-deadly-flood\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-29T15:00:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Their whole village has disappeared’: frantic hunt for survivors in Kathmandu hospital",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/nepal-flood-missing-kathmandu-hospital",
      "description": "<p>Family members pin photos of Nepal’s missing to hospital wall as people try not to give up hope on loved ones</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/aug/29/nepal-tibet-floods-latest-updates-death-toll-missing-search-and-rescue\">Nepal-Tibet flash flood – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Posters of missing people line the wall of the hospital, the glue still fresh beneath. A schoolgirl smiling in her uniform; a beaming, chubby-cheeked baby; a couple smiling on their wedding day; a young man, hands on hips, atop a mountain peak; a young girl with flowing hair, peaking out from behind a door.</p><p>These faces are just a fraction of the thousands who have not been seen since deadly flash floods coursed through the Himalayas and wiped away entire villages. By Saturday morning, the toll of the missing had risen to almost 3,000, in both Nepal and Tibet.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/29/nepal-flood-missing-kathmandu-hospital\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-29T14:11:10"
    }
  ]
